\f0 \b \fs28 \pard \s11 \li1209 \fi-1007 \ri1007 \ql Class Description \
\fs14\
\f1 \b0 \fs28 \pard \s4 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 NSDecimalNumberHandler is a class that adopts the NSDecimalNumberBehaviors protocol. This class allows you to set the way an NSDecimalNumber rounds off and handles errors, without having to create a custom class. \
\fs14\
\fs28 You can use an instance of this class as an argument to any of the NSDecimalNumber methods that end with the word \b ...Behavior:\b0 . If you don\'27t think you need special behavior, you probably don\'27t need this class. The odds are that NSDecimalNumber\'27s default behavior will suit your needs.\
\fs14\
\fs28 For more information, see the NSDecimalNumberBehaviors protocol specification.\
\fs14\
