\s40 \li2520 \fi-604 \f1 \b0 \fs28 +\'80(NSDecimalNumberHandler\'80*)\b defaultDecimalNumberHandler\
\fs14\
\b0 \fs28 \pard \s4 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Creates and returns the default instance of NSDecimalNumberHandler. \
\fs14\
\fs28 This instance does not round numbers off. It assumes that your need for precision does not exceed 38 significant digits. And it raises an exception when its NSDecimalNumber tries to divide by zero, or when its NSDecimalNumber produces a number that is too big or small to be represented. \
\fs14\
