\fs14\
\i0 \fs28 \pard \s4 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Creates and returns an NSDecimalNumberHandler with customized behavior. \
\fs14\
\fs28 \i scale\i0  and \i roundingMode\i0  affect the way the NSDecimalNumberHandler\'27s NSDecimalNumber rounds off its return value. \i scale\i0  sets the number of digits a rounded value should have after its decimal point.\i  roundingMode\i0  sets the rule by which that NSDecimalNumbers are rounded off; \i roundingMode\i0  has four possiblevalues: NSRoundUp, NSRoundDown, NSRoundPlain, and NSRoundBankers.\
\fs14\
\fs28 The \i raiseOn...\i0  arguments determine whether the NSDecimalNumberHandler will raise an exception when its NSDecimalNumber notifies it of a certain kind of calculation error. If a \i raiseOn...\i0  argument is YES, NSDecimalNumberHandler will raise an exception; if a \i raiseOn.. \i0 argument is NO, NSDecimalNumber will ignore the error, and return control to the calling method.\
\fs14\
\fs28 See the NSDecimalNumberBehaviors protocol spectification for a complete explanation of these possible behaviors.\
\fs14\
